From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a PDF drawn smaller keeps its thin strokes

The viewer renders a page bitmap at the device scale and draws it into the
page with nearest-neighbor sampling, which is right only at 1:1. On a desk
with monitors at several densities, cc rasters the page smaller for each
monitor below the highest one (patch 0072), so the bitmap is downscaled:
nearest-neighbor keeps whole source columns or drops them, and thin strokes
in text break up.

- `PdfViewWebPlugin::Paint` draws the snapshot with linear, mipmapped
  sampling. A downscale filters; at 1:1 the pixels are the same.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`. `guard-pdf-scaled-text.sh` checks it.
---
 pdf/pdf_view_web_plugin.cc | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pdf/pdf_view_web_plugin.cc b/pdf/pdf_view_web_plugin.cc
index 81f6d1e..1dccd9d 100644
--- a/pdf/pdf_view_web_plugin.cc
+++ b/pdf/pdf_view_web_plugin.cc
@@ -104,6 +104,7 @@
 #include "third_party/skia/include/core/SkImageInfo.h"
 #include "third_party/skia/include/core/SkRect.h"
 #include "third_party/skia/include/core/SkRefCnt.h"
+#include "third_party/skia/include/core/SkSamplingOptions.h"
 #include "third_party/skia/include/core/SkSize.h"
 #include "ui/base/cursor/cursor.h"
 #include "ui/base/cursor/mojom/cursor_type.mojom-shared.h"
@@ -713,7 +714,14 @@ void PdfViewWebPlugin::Paint(cc::PaintCanvas* canvas, const gfx::Rect& rect) {
     canvas->scale(snapshot_scale_, snapshot_scale_);
   }
 
-  canvas->drawImage(snapshot_, 0, 0);
+  // Domicile's engine fork: cc rasters this page smaller than the snapshot
+  // on a monitor below the desk's highest density. Nearest-neighbor sampling
+  // drops whole columns there, and thin strokes in text with them; a
+  // mipmapped, filtered downscale keeps them. At 1:1 it draws the same pixels.
+  canvas->drawImage(snapshot_, 0, 0,
+                    SkSamplingOptions(SkFilterMode::kLinear,
+                                      SkMipmapMode::kLinear),
+                    nullptr);
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_PDF_INK2)
   if (!ink_module_) {
-- 
